<title>USA: Compaq, Tandem waiting period ends.</title>
<headline>Compaq, Tandem waiting period ends.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Compaq Computer Corp said Tuesday that the waiting period under the Hart-Scott-Rodino anti-trust law has expired in connection with its planned acquisition of Tandem Computers Inc.</p>
<p>The announcement came the same day that the European Commission cleared the acquisition.</p>
<p>The transaction is subject to the approval of Tandem's shareholders. If approved, the transaction is expected to close shortly after an August 29 meeting of shareholders that has been scheduled.</p>
<p>Compaq is one of the world's largest suppliers of computer products. Tandem is a supplier of computer processing systems for operations in banks, stock exchanges and telecommunications.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
